<title>SINGAPORE: Broadway 1996 net profit falls 52.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Broadway 1996 net profit falls 52.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Dec 31 1996</p>
<p>	     (in million of Singapore $ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			 0.52   vs    1.10</p>
<p>    Group shares (cents)	   0.45   vs    0.96</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)		 0.40   vs    0.40</p>
<p>    Turnover			  60.72   vs   50.67</p>
<p>    Other income incl interest   0.09   vs    0.12</p>
<p>    Interest expense		 1.71   vs    1.06</p>
<p>    Depreciation		     5.98   vs    3.39</p>
<p>    Operating pretax loss	  0.18   vs    1.67 (gain)</p>
<p>    Associates		(gain) 1.36   vs    0.05 (loss)</p>
<p>    Tax				  0.71   vs    0.54</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries		  nil    vs    0.52 (loss)</p>
<p>Note - Broadway Industries  Group Ltd is an investment holding group involved in making and selling of foam, pulp and vacuum-formed packing products.</p>
<p>--Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
